INTERPRETATION: a PSD Gram matrix was found for the LEAST-SQUARES-FITTED quartic approximant to F's quartic behaviour at A_18. This is additional numerical evidence (not a proof: the fit comes from noisy high-precision finite-difference samples, not an exact symbolic derivation) that the fitted quartic is non-negative on the entire near-null subspace, not just at the sampled rays. It does not put Conjecture (Multi-Direction Positivity) at A_18 on an elementary footing: what settles that conjecture is the classification cited in Corollary 7.31.
